#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064343 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063983 :question/id #uuid "3138f267-3903-510c-86e8-5597d3689262" :question/math-academy-id "e-143" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y = x^4 + 3\\sqrt [3]{x^2}$ at the point $(1,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4}+3{x}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {x}^{3}+3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {x}^{-1/3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{-1/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & =4(1{)}^{3}+2(1{)}^{-1/3} \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $6.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510700 :question-generator/id #uuid "a32ff939-77c4-521a-a83a-e54ec25d64f3" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186064343.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80bd3d5d-7aff-5a42-83fa-ba1927818c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061400} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a16a6b-137a-50c0-a444-9c3d7b17a6c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11^{1/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061401} {:answer/id #uuid "c0df2c06-5a97-51cc-812f-585c9b0aa742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061402} {:answer/id #uuid "d03708dc-5360-52e2-a9f1-9f68380cd166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061403} {:answer/id #uuid "31d8aef9-b933-5d60-89a9-ac2c