\  & =20+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{62}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{62}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38eb4046-4c7a-5ac7-8681-c5433d9c769b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38eb4046-4c7a-5ac7-8681-c5433d9c769b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295590} :answer-field/id #uuid "765ee05d-d577-5c70-860a-1a3a3269b893" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296877}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d2746f0-484f-5af7-8356-aa63ec30ff54" :question/math-academy-id "q-304130" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=4x-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(4,12).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-2{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =4-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & =4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,12)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0248b104-41da-5e1a-bb16-676e3f8b4e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186